{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>No man</b>. And even if one knew when he would die, how would it benefit him? For there is no man who has the power to imprison the spirit. And this verse shows that the spirit is, so to speak, imprisoned in a prison, as I began at the beginning of my words." "<b>And there is no dominion</b>. Kingship does not avail the king, nor does weaponry ready for battle and for sortie — like 'weaponry,' and similarly וחיתו מעבור בשלח, meaning a battle sortie. Some interpret 'in battle' as the battle of the constitution that guards the body until the time of its end against illness that enters the body, and if the constitution weakens, a man dies." "<b>And the meaning of 'wicked'</b>. Most movement and victory, as in 'He quieteth — and who can condemn?' and 'whichever way he turns, he acts wickedly.' Some interpret that it refers to wealth, most of which is gathered from wickedness."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {1 "The phrase וחיתו מעבור בשלח appears to be a partial biblical quotation, possibly from Job; the surrounding syntax is compressed and the reference is left unresolved."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:28.080756498Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}